---
import InfoLayout from '../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
---

<InfoLayout title="Frequently Asked Questions | FreeOnlineToolkit" description="Find answers to common questions about FreeOnlineToolkit.org — our free online calculators, accuracy, privacy, guide content, and how to get the most out of our tools.">
  <h1 class="animate-in">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1"><em>Last updated: May 2026</em></p>

  <h2 class="animate-in"><i class="fa-solid fa-calculator"></i> About Our Tools</h2>

  <h3 class="animate-in">Are the calculators really free?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">Yes, all calculators and tools on FreeOnlineToolkit.org are completely free to use. There are no paywalls, no subscription fees, no hidden charges, and no usage limits. You can use every tool as many times as you need, for any purpose. We do not require you to create an account or provide any personal information to use any calculator on the site.</p>

  <h3 class="animate-in">Do I need to sign up or create an account?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">No. None of our tools require registration, login, or account creation. Simply visit the tool page, enter your values, and get your results instantly. Your privacy is important to us — all calculations run entirely in your browser, and your data never leaves your device.</p>

  <h3 class="animate-in">How accurate are your calculators?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">Our calculators use standard formulas verified against authoritative sources. Financial calculators follow industry-standard formulas used by banks and financial institutions. Health calculators use clinically validated methods from peer-reviewed medical research. Conversion tools use official measurement standards from organizations like NIST. Each tool page includes a methodology section explaining the formula used and links to references where applicable.</p>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">While we strive for accuracy, our tools are designed for educational and planning purposes. Always verify critical financial, medical, or legal decisions with a qualified professional who can evaluate your specific circumstances.</p>

  <h3 class="animate-in">What types of calculators do you offer?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">We currently offer over 89 free calculators and tools across 16 categories. Our financial calculators cover mortgages, loans, investments, savings, and retirement planning. Health and wellness tools include BMI, body fat, calorie, due date, and ideal weight calculators. We also offer utility tools like a password generator, currency converter, QR code generator, unit converter, and time zone converter. Business tools cover startup valuation, SaaS metrics, freelance rates, and employee costs.</p>

  <h3 class="animate-in">How do you ensure your calculators stay up to date?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">Our editorial team monitors authoritative sources for changes that affect our tools. When the IRS releases new tax brackets, when the CDC updates health guidelines, or when the Federal Reserve adjusts interest rates, we update the affected calculators and content accordingly. Each tool page displays a "last updated" date so you can see when it was most recently reviewed. We maintain a rolling review schedule to ensure all tools remain current.</p>

  <h2 class="animate-in"><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i> Privacy &amp; Data</h2>

  <h3 class="animate-in">Do you store my calculation data?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">No. All calculations are performed entirely in your browser using JavaScript. Your inputs and results never leave your device. We do not store, transmit, or have access to any numbers you enter into our calculators. This means your financial information, health data, and personal details remain completely private.</p>

  <h3 class="animate-in">What information do you collect?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">We collect minimal anonymous usage data through Google Analytics, including page views, browser type, and approximate geographic location (city or country level only). This data is aggregated and cannot identify you personally. We use it to understand which tools are most popular and how visitors navigate the site, which helps us improve the user experience.</p>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">We also display advertisements via Google AdSense, which may use cookies to serve relevant ads. You can manage your ad personalization preferences at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ad Settings</a>. For full details, see our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

  <h3 class="animate-in">Do you sell my data?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">No. We do not sell, rent, or share personal information with third parties. The only third-party services we use are Google Analytics (for anonymous usage statistics) and Google AdSense (for advertisements). Both services have their own privacy policies, and you can opt out of personalized advertising through your Google account settings.</p>

  <h2 class="animate-in"><i class="fa-regular fa-compass"></i> Using the Guides</h2>

  <h3 class="animate-in">What are the guides for?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">Our guides provide in-depth educational content about the topics our tools cover. Each guide explains the underlying concepts, formulas, and practical applications in plain language. They are designed to help you understand not just what the result is, but what it means and how to use it. We currently offer 22 guides covering topics from mortgage planning to password security, with more being added regularly.</p>

  <h3 class="animate-in">Can I trust the information in the guides?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">Our guides are researched and written with attention to accuracy. We cite authoritative sources including government agencies (IRS, CDC, CFPB), international organizations (WHO), and peer-reviewed research. Each guide is reviewed periodically and updated when guidelines or regulations change. If you find an error or have a suggestion, please contact us through our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>

  <h2 class="animate-in"><i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question"></i> Technical Questions</h2>

  <h3 class="animate-in">Which browsers do your tools support?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">Our tools work on all modern browsers including Chrome, Firefox, Safari, and Edge. They are tested on both desktop and mobile devices. If you encounter any issues, make sure your browser is updated to the latest version. Some older browsers may not support the JavaScript features our calculators use.</p>

  <h3 class="animate-in">Do your tools work on mobile phones?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">Yes. All tools are fully responsive and work on smartphones, tablets, and desktop browsers. The interface adjusts to your screen size for comfortable use on any device. Simply visit the tool page on your mobile browser and use it the same way you would on a desktop.</p>

  <h3 class="animate-in">What happens if I reload the page?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">Reloading the page will reset the calculator to its default values. Your current inputs and results will be lost, as we do not store calculation data on servers. If you want to save your results, take a screenshot or note down the key numbers before reloading or navigating away.</p>

  <h2 class="animate-in"><i class="fa-regular fa-lightbulb"></i> Suggestions &amp; Feedback</h2>

  <h3 class="animate-in">How can I suggest a new tool?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">We welcome tool suggestions! Send us a message through our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> with a description of the calculator you would like to see, what problem it should solve, and who would use it. We review every suggestion and prioritize tools that would help the widest audience. Popular requests that are practical to implement are added to our development roadmap.</p>

  <h3 class="animate-in">I found a bug. What should I do?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">Please report it through our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> with as much detail as possible — the name of the tool, the inputs you entered, what you expected to happen, what actually happened, and your browser and operating system. Bug reports with detailed reproduction steps can usually be resolved within a few days.</p>

  <h3 class="animate-in">How long does it take to add a new feature or fix a bug?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">Bug fixes are prioritized based on severity. Critical issues affecting calculator accuracy are addressed as quickly as possible, typically within 24-48 hours. Minor bugs and feature requests are scheduled based on our development roadmap. We appreciate your patience and your contribution to improving the site.</p>

  <h2 class="animate-in"><i class="fa-regular fa-building"></i> About the Site</h2>

  <h3 class="animate-in">Who runs FreeOnlineToolkit.org?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">FreeOnlineToolkit.org is an independent project created by developers and content creators who believe that essential calculation tools should be accessible to everyone without cost or barriers. We are not affiliated with any financial institution, healthcare provider, or government agency. Our mission is to provide fast, accurate, and completely free online calculators for everyday needs.</p>

  <h3 class="animate-in">How is the site funded?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">The site is funded through non-intrusive advertisements served by Google AdSense. These ads help cover hosting costs, development, and content creation. We carefully choose ad formats that do not interfere with the user experience or the functionality of our tools. We do not accept paid placements that would compromise the accuracy or impartiality of our calculators or editorial content.</p>

  <h3 class="animate-in">Do you add new tools regularly?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">Yes. We regularly add new tools based on user requests and emerging needs. Our roadmap includes calculators for additional financial scenarios, health metrics, business planning, and everyday utility tasks. Follow the site or check back periodically to see what is new. If you have a specific request, let us know through our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>

  <h3 class="animate-in">How can I contact you?</h3>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">You can reach us through our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> or by emailing vxeexoffical@gmail.com. We typically respond within 24-48 hours during business days. Bug reports and accuracy concerns are prioritized for faster response.</p>
</InfoLayout>
